  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0016_a45f8a9feb5d.png\">\r\n\r\nIn alkaline medium the acidic proton present in the molecule is abstracted to give enolate ion. In the next step hydroxide ion if present at $\\beta$ -position leaves giving $\\alpha-\\beta$ unsaturated carbonyl compound. In (a), (c) and\r\n(d), dehydration cannot take place due to improper placement of groups."
